{:id :EACL-FORMAL-014
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :lore-resource-refinement-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "subproblem-cache/parent-future/child-future/inherited-same-key"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :resource-bound
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 worktree before context-aware recursive-self execution"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "A recursive same-key `resolve!` bypassed its shared flight by invoking `compute` directly. Clojure futures inherit dynamic bindings, so a child thread could inherit the parent's resolving-key set, take the self-bypass, and run a callback that was absent from the coordinator's active-callback count."
 :fix
 "Recursive self-bypass now executes through `with-computation-slot`. That function reuses the permit only when the current execution context is the recorded owner; an inherited child context acquires its own global permit. Recursive bypass still creates no second shared flight."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.subproblem-cache-test/inherited-same-key-self-bypass-acquires-a-child-slot-test"
  "formal mutation :inherited-self-bypass-skips-computation-slot"
  "formal/dafny/SubproblemCache.dfy context-qualified recursive bypass lemmas"]}
